 "about": "Living people the Champagne houses tab never names: in prose, in a source's title or in a source's address (codex59). The Flagships tab's list (.scripts/flagships/people.json) and the Grapes tab's living writers are refused as well, so a name already there is not repeated here. A house and a cuvée keep their names: the record's own house, its cuvée and its second cuvée are taken out of a string before it is read, so Pol Roger, Nicolas Feuillatte and Sir Winston Churchill stand as the labels they are. A name here only refuses: it is never proof that a person may be named, and the long dead are named with their dates from two sources. It grows as authors and refuters meet more: add the name in the same commit as the record that met it.",
